From: AdobeWine
Subject: [PATCH] mspatcha: Normalize and transform 32-bit PE files.

Adopted from LinDobe (le-birnes/LinDobe, LGPL-2.1+), patch 0097, with these changes: none to the code; it applies to Wine 11.10 without fuzz; diff regenerated with diff -u against our tree.

Upstream mspatcha could not apply PA19 deltas made for 32-bit executables. It refused every delta with a rift
table (the per-file "unknown count"). It matched old files by their raw CRC, but the patch creator takes that CRC
after normalization (rebase to the new image base, new COFF timestamp, unbinding, lock prefixes, checksum). It read
the header's rebase field as a single VLI where it is a 16-bit image base plus a COFF timestamp, and it skipped
the resource timestamp. It refused old files larger than the LZX window, and NormalizeFileForPatchSignature was
a stub. Acrobat DC's update has 1218 deltas with rift tables.

The header is now read in full (second option field with transform bits and optional window size, image base,
COFF and resource timestamps, rift tables). Old files are normalized before matching. An old file that already is
the new file, exactly or after normalization, is returned as it is. When a delta has a rift table, the
normalized old file goes through the rift transform before it is used as the LZX dictionary: relocations or an
address scan, imports, exports, near jumps and calls, and resource directories are moved to their new RVAs. Only
the first window of a large old file is the dictionary, and the decoder takes the window size from the caller.
NormalizeFileForPatchSignature is implemented. The PE work is in the new file pe.c.

Rewritten from a behaviour specification; checked black-box against Windows' mspatcha.dll output. Where the
specification was unclear or wrong, the Windows DLL's results decided. The specification came from a study of Windows'
mspatcha.dll that included decompiling it, and the first version of this code was based on that study. A separate
session of the same AI tool wrote this version without access to the decompile or the first version. That is not a
clean-room process, and it is not independent proof that no Microsoft code carried over. The file and handle interfaces treat a normalized already-patched file like an exact
one under APPLY_OPTION_FAIL_IF_EXACT and ignore APPLY_OPTION_FAIL_IF_CLOSE there. A malformed lock-prefix table
ends normalization (no checksum; NormalizeFileForPatchSignature returns 0). A HIGHADJ relocation that ends a block
keeps the rebase reading entries up to the end of the file.
Test: dlls/mspatcha/tests: 2145 tests, 0 failures (x86_64 and i386).
Test: wine/tests/mspatcha/applypatch.c builtin on Acrobat DC's 3544 deltas (installers/acro-x/all-wine.txt): 3534
ok, 10 failed (the VC runtime deltas Windows also fails, ERROR_PATCH_WRONG_FILE); all 3534 outputs byte-identical
to Windows' mspatcha.dll output.
Test: NormalizeFileForPatchSignature output and return value identical to Windows' for 148 code-bearing PE32 files
and 33 edited edge-case files under several option sets. The AXE8SharedExpat.dll delta applied to its own new
file returns it unchanged, as on Windows.

Lab (acrobat-adopt, 2026-11-08, runtime 11.10-185ad = 185 + riched20-textpara-getters + unsecapp-wmi-sink-host
+ this set): Acrobat Pro installed the user's way (`neutron programs install` of the Acrobat setup.exe = AcroPro.msi +
AcrobatDCx64Upd2600222031.msp) into a fresh copy of a signed-in Adobe prefix: "Setup Completed", installed 26.002.22031,
7778 files, 1.8 GB, thorvg-1.dll present (n=1). Before this set every install ended 1603 at PatchFiles (AcMsp-1..9).
PROVENANCE (decision for Nuck before import): the description above states that the specification came from a study
that decompiled Windows' mspatcha.dll, that the first version was based on it, and that this is not a clean-room
process. Neutron's own mspatcha patches (mspatcha-pa19-pe-transform, -large-reference, -already-patched; black-box
only, 3526 of 3544) are the alternative this replaces. Both findings of ours are present here (only the first window of
an old file larger than the window is the reference; an already-patched old file with APPLY_OPTION_FAIL_IF_EXACT
returns ERROR_PATCH_NOT_NECESSARY).
Harness (all 3544 PA19 deltas of AcrobatDCx64Upd2600222031.msp through ApplyPatchToFileW, acrobat-msp's applytest):
x86_64 3534/10 and i386 3534/10, n=2 each, identical; the 10 = VC++ runtime CC943011/E281B893 copies whose old file in
this MSI is not the delta's target (ERROR_PATCH_WRONG_FILE, the same 10 that fail with ours). Our three patches
3526/18; stock 185 2322/1222 (same harness, same prefix). 0 regressions against ours.
Kill switch: none (the module is replaced as a whole; the A/B arm is stock mspatcha in the same harness).
---
--- a/dlls/mspatcha/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/mspatcha/Makefile.in
@@ -9,4 +9,5 @@
 SOURCES = \
 	lzxd_dec.c \
 	mspatcha_main.c \
-	pa19.c
+	pa19.c \
+	pe.c
--- a/dlls/mspatcha/lzxd_dec.c
+++ b/dlls/mspatcha/lzxd_dec.c
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@
 #define MAX_CHUNK_UNCOMPRESSED_SIZE 0x8000
 #define E8_TRANSFORM_LIMIT_BITS 30
 #define E8_TRANSFORM_DEAD_ZONE 10
+#define MIN_WINDOW_SIZE ((size_t)1 << 15)
 
 struct LZXD_dec {
     /* use byte pointers instead of uint16 for simplicity on uncompressed
@@ -662,7 +663,7 @@
 DWORD decode_lzxd_stream(const BYTE *src, const size_t input_size,
     BYTE *dst, const size_t output_size,
     const size_t predef_size,
-    DWORD large_window,
+    const size_t window_size,
     PPATCH_PROGRESS_CALLBACK progress_fn,
     PVOID  progress_ctx)
 {
@@ -692,29 +693,18 @@
     dec->reps[1] = 1;
     dec->reps[2] = 1;
 
-    /* apparently the window size is not recorded and must be deduced from the file sizes */
+    /* the window size decides the number of distance slots */
     {
-        unsigned max_window = large_window ? MAX_LARGE_WINDOW : MAX_NORMAL_WINDOW;
-        size_t window = (size_t)1 << 17;
-        /* round up the old file size per the lzxd spec - correctness verified by fuzz tests */
-        size_t total = (predef_size + 0x7FFF) & ~0x7FFF;
-        unsigned delta;
+        size_t window = min(max(window_size, MIN_WINDOW_SIZE), MAX_LARGE_WINDOW);
+        unsigned bits = 15;
 
-        total += output_size;
-        dec->dist_slot_count = 34;
-        while (window < total && window < ((size_t)1 << 19))
-        {
-            dec->dist_slot_count += 2;
-            window <<= 1;
-        }
-        delta = 4;
-        while (window < total && window < max_window)
-        {
-            dec->dist_slot_count += delta;
-            delta <<= 1;
-            window <<= 1;
-        }
-        TRACE("setting window to 0x%X\n", (unsigned)window);
+        while (((size_t)1 << bits) < window)
+            ++bits;
+        if (bits <= 19)
+            dec->dist_slot_count = bits * 2;
+        else
+            dec->dist_slot_count = 38 + 4 * ((1u << (bits - 19)) - 1);
+        TRACE("setting window to 0x%X\n", 1u << bits);
     }
 
     dec->bit_pos = 0;
--- a/dlls/mspatcha/lzxd_dec.h
+++ b/dlls/mspatcha/lzxd_dec.h
@@ -22,6 +22,6 @@
 DWORD decode_lzxd_stream(const BYTE *src, const size_t input_size,
     BYTE *dst, const size_t output_size,
     const size_t predef_size,
-    DWORD large_window,
+    const size_t window_size,
     PPATCH_PROGRESS_CALLBACK progress_fn,
     PVOID  progress_ctx);
--- a/dlls/mspatcha/mspatcha_main.c
+++ b/dlls/mspatcha/mspatcha_main.c
@@ -19,14 +19,8 @@
  * Foundation, Inc., 51 Franklin St, Fifth Floor, Boston, MA 02110-1301, USA
  *
  * TODO
- *  - Special processing of 32-bit executables is not supported, so this
- *    version cannot patch 32-bit .exe and .dll files. See pa19.c for details.
- *  - Implement interleaved decoding when PATCH_OPTION_INTERLEAVE_FILES was
- *    used or the old file exceeds the lzxd window size.
- *  - APPLY_OPTION_FAIL_IF_CLOSE is ignored. Normalization of 32-bit PE files
- *    is required for checking this.
- *  - GetFilePatchSignature* and NormalizeFileForPatchSignature require a
- *    solution to the above 32-bit exe problem.
+ *  - Implement interleaved decoding when PATCH_OPTION_INTERLEAVE_FILES was used.
+ *  - GetFilePatchSignature* are not implemented.
  */
 
 #include <stdarg.h>
@@ -265,8 +259,43 @@
     ULONG new_coff_base, ULONG new_coff_time, ULONG ignore_range_count, PPATCH_IGNORE_RANGE ignore_range,
     ULONG retain_range_count, PPATCH_RETAIN_RANGE retain_range)
 {
-    FIXME("stub - %p, %lu, %lx, %p, %lu, %lu, %lu, %p, %lu, %p\n", file_buffer, file_size, flags, options, new_coff_base,
+    BYTE *buf = file_buffer;
+    enum pe_normalize_result res;
+    BOOL changed;
+    ULONG i;
+
+    TRACE("%p, %lu, %lx, %p, %lu, %lu, %lu, %p, %lu, %p\n", file_buffer, file_size, flags, options, new_coff_base,
         new_coff_time, ignore_range_count, ignore_range, retain_range_count, retain_range);
-    SetLastError(ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED);
-    return 0;
+
+    /* returns 1 if unchanged, 2 if changed, 0 if the image is malformed */
+    if (buf == NULL || file_size == 0)
+        return 1;
+
+    res = pe_normalize(buf, file_size, flags, new_coff_base, new_coff_time);
+    /* nothing more is done to a malformed image */
+    if (res == PE_MALFORMED)
+        return 0;
+    changed = (res == PE_CHANGED);
+
+    /* ranges which do not lie wholly inside the buffer are left alone */
+    for (i = 0; i < ignore_range_count; ++i)
+    {
+        if (ignore_range[i].OffsetInOldFile <= file_size
+            && ignore_range[i].LengthInBytes <= file_size - ignore_range[i].OffsetInOldFile)
+        {
+            memset(buf + ignore_range[i].OffsetInOldFile, 0, ignore_range[i].LengthInBytes);
+            changed = TRUE;
+        }
+    }
+    for (i = 0; i < retain_range_count; ++i)
+    {
+        if (retain_range[i].OffsetInOldFile <= file_size
+            && retain_range[i].LengthInBytes <= file_size - retain_range[i].OffsetInOldFile)
+        {
+            memset(buf + retain_range[i].OffsetInOldFile, 0, retain_range[i].LengthInBytes);
+            changed = TRUE;
+        }
+    }
+
+    return changed ? 2 : 1;
 }
--- a/dlls/mspatcha/pa19.c
+++ b/dlls/mspatcha/pa19.c
@@ -17,19 +17,12 @@
  * License along with this library; if not, write to the Free Software
  * Foundation, Inc., 51 Franklin St, Fifth Floor, Boston, MA 02110-1301, USA
  *
+ * Old files which are 32-bit PE images are normalized before their CRC is
+ * checked, and transformed using the patch's rift table before they are used
+ * as the LZX dictionary. See pe.c.
+ *
  * TODO
- * - Normalization of 32-bit PE executable files and reversal of special
- *   processing of these executables is not implemented.
- *   Without normalization, old files cannot be validated for patching. The
- *   function NormalizeFileForPatchSignature() in Windows could be used to work
- *   out exactly how normalization works.
- *   Most/all of the special processing seems to be relocation of targets for
- *   some jump/call instructions to match more of the old file and improve
- *   compression. Patching of 64-bit exes works because mspatchc.dll does not
- *   implement special processing of them. In 32-bit patches, the variable
- *   named here 'unknown_count' seems to indicate presence of data related to
- *   reversing the processing. The changes that must be reversed occur at some,
- *   but not all, of the positions listed in the PE .reloc table.
+ * - Interleaved files (PATCH_OPTION_INTERLEAVE_FILES) are not supported.
  */
 
 #include <stdarg.h>
@@ -49,6 +42,13 @@
 #define PA19_FILE_MAGIC 0x39314150
 #define PATCH_OPTION_EXTRA_FLAGS 0x80000000
 
+/* bits of the second option field: the transform bits (see pe.c) and the
+ * presence of a window size field */
+#define PATCH_OPTION_2_WINDOW_SIZE 0x00010000
+#define PATCH_OPTION_2_SUPPORTED_FLAGS (0x0000033f | PATCH_OPTION_2_WINDOW_SIZE)
+
+#define MIN_DERIVED_WINDOW 0x20000
+
 static UINT32 compute_zero_crc32(UINT32 crc, INT_PTR len)
 {
     static const BYTE zero_buffer[1024];
@@ -68,9 +68,14 @@
  *  UINT32 options;
